# =============================================================================
# Store — DELETE requests (VS Code REST Client) — DELETE /api/v1/stores/{id} (ADMIN)
# =============================================================================
# Semantics (ticket 0007, Q8): DELETE is SOFT — it flips status to DELETED and
# returns 204. The row is NEVER removed (history keeps a valid reference).
# BLOCKED (temporarily closed) and DELETED (gone) are different states.
# Deleting twice is idempotent (both 204). Revival via update is legal — no
# terminality is enforced.
#
# How to run:
#   1. Start the backend: `docker compose up -d --build` — http://localhost:4000
#   2. Click the "Send Request" CodeLens above any request below.
#
# Prerequisites: an admin persona (see http/store/create.http header for the
# SQL promotion one-liner).
#
# Notes:
#   - Run top-to-bottom on first use — later requests assume earlier ones ran.
#   - All data is FAKE. The automated suite: StoreApiTests (src/test/java).
#   - Access tokens expire after 15 MINUTES. If tokened requests suddenly 401,
#     re-send request 1 (admin login) to refresh the chained tokens, then continue.
#   - Re-running: request 2 returns 409 (brand persists) — harmless.
#   - Expected codes: 204 deleted (idempotent), 200 post-delete read shows
#     status DELETED, 401 no/invalid token, 403 non-admin, 404 unknown id,
#     405 wrong method.
# =============================================================================

@storeUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/stores
@authUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth

### 1 — Setup: login the admin persona
# Expected: 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2 — Setup: create a store to delete
# Expected: 201
# @name createStore
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Doomed Store",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{adminLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "12 Market Road, Lagos",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "doomed-store@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 3 — Delete it
# Expected: 204 — no body
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4 — Delete it AGAIN (idempotent)
# Expected: 204 — deleting a DELETED store is a no-op that still succeeds
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 5 — Fetch it after deletion
# Expected: 200 with status DELETED — the soft-delete contract, visible
GET {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 6 — No Authorization header
# Expected: 401
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}

### 7 — Garbage token
# Expected: 401
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-jwt

### 8 — Setup: signup a regular persona
# Expected: 201 (409 if she already exists — either way the account exists)
# @name regularSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Bola Deleteless",
  "email": "bola.deleteless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234573"
}

### 9 — Setup: login the regular persona
# Expected: 200
# @name regularLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bola.deleteless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 10 — Delete as a regular user
# Expected: 403 — deletion is admin-only
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{regularLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 11 — Unknown id
# Expected: 404 — "Store not found"
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 12 — Wrong method: POST against the store path
# Expected: 405 — Allow: GET, PUT, DELETE
POST {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 13 — Revive the deleted store via update (data recovery is legal)
# Expected: 200 — status flips back to ACTIVE; no terminality enforced
PUT {{storeUrl}}/{{createStore.response.body.publicId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}
